  <translations>
    <en>
      <description>Rain Bird 100-DVF-TBOS is a 1″ solenoid valve with flow control and a 9 V latching solenoid for battery-powered controllers. Flow adjustment helps limit delivery to suit the irrigation zone, while manual operation simplifies checks and servicing. Suitable for automatic irrigation in gardens and landscaped areas. Series specifications: operating pressure approximately 1.0–10.4 bar; flow up to about 9.1 m³/h; 9 V DC solenoid.</description>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>b0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>b00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>100-DVF-TBOS</text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>b01</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text> — a 1″ diaphragm solenoid valve for automatic irrigation.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Purpose and operating principle</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The controller energises the solenoid, which operates the diaphragm and opens the water passage. When the signal stops, the valve closes automatically. The DV/DVF series is designed for automatic irrigation in gardens and professional landscaped areas. Its diaphragm mechanism controls flow through a pilot circuit.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Construction and model-specific features</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The model includes manual flow control. The 9 V DC latching solenoid requires a compatible battery controller and must not be connected to a 24 VAC output.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Hydraulic and electrical specifications</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>Size 1″; operating pressure 1,0–10,4 bar; flow 0,05–9,1 m³/h; solenoid 9 V DC latching. Actual flow depends on pipe, filter and fitting losses as well as available pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Installation, adjustment and maintenance</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Connection: 1″ female thread at inlet and outlet. Before installation, confirm flow direction, operating pressure and thread standard. Fit the valve in an accessible valve box and flush the pipework before commissioning. During service, inspect the diaphragm, pilot filter, solenoid and seals. For flows below 0.68 m³/h or drip irrigation, the manufacturer recommends a 200-mesh (75 μm) upstream filter.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Check flow direction and stay within the permitted operating pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
        <listItem>bullet</listItem>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Flush pipework before connection to keep sand and swarf out of the pilot circuit.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
        <listItem>bullet</listItem>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Leave access for future maintenance.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
        <listItem>bullet</listItem>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h5</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
